-- Test Case Design: Password Field Validation
-- Using Equivalence Partitioning (EP) & Boundary Value Analysis (BVA)

-- 1. Objective

-- Design a complete, defensible set of test cases for the Password field on a login/registration form, 
   using two core black-box test design techniques:

-- Equivalence Partitioning (EP) — divides input data into classes that the system is expected to treat identically, 
   so we test one representative value per class instead of every possible value.

-- Boundary Value Analysis (BVA) — extends EP by targeting the edges of each partition, 
   since defects statistically cluster at boundaries (off-by-one errors, < vs <=, incorrect loop limits, etc.).

-- Login password field validation :- 
-- Requirement :- Password field must have 8-16 character. Any input outside this range must be rejected with validation error.
-- Field :-  Password 
-- Rule 1  :-   8<= length(password) <=16
-- Rule 2 :-  Must contain at least one special character
-- Type :- Mandatory field, string input

-- Equivalance Partitioning-

| Test. ID | Description | Input | Length | Range | Expected Result |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **EVP_01** | Password less than minimum range | Pass9! | 6 | 0-7 Charcter | Rejected - password must be 8-16 characters |
| **EVP_02** | Password within accepted range, without special charaters | Password123 | 11 | 8-16 Character | Rejected - Must contain special characters |
| **EVP_03** | Password within accepted range, with special charaters | Password@123 | 12 | 8-16 Character | Accepted |
| **EVP_04** | Password more than max. range | Password123ABCDEF | 17 | 17+ Character | Rejected - password must be 8-16 characters |

-- Boundary value Analysis

-- Minimum -  8 (min-1, min, min+1)
-- Maximum - 16(max-1, max, max+1)
-- Total - 6 test cases"	

| Test case ID | Boundary value | Input | length | Region | Expected Result |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **BV_01** | Lower limit -1 | Passwor | 7 | Just below lower limit | Rejected |
| **BV_02** | Lower limit | Password | 8 | Lower limit (valid min range) | Accepted |
| **BV_03** | Lower limit +1 | Password@ | 9 | Just above lower limit | Accepted |
| **BV_04** | Upper Limit -1 | Password@123456 | 15 | Just below upper limit | Accepted |
| **BV_05** | Upper limit | Password@123457 | 16 | Upper limit (Valid max range) | Accepted |
| **BV_06** | Upper limit +1 | Password@12345678 | 17 | Just abover upper limit | Rejected |

